{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791389660,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_202610080014167a3726ddabfd4540\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: outline(name), read_method(name, method, class), write_method(name, method, source - one METHOD block, class), read_object(name, include main|testclasses), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: prefer outline, read_method and write_method for changing existing methods; use write_source only for new methods, changed declarations or a new test include, and then write the FULL source; read before write; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG (settings from pia.env), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"TheThe bug: pia.env parsing doesn't strip trailing comments from values. Let me look at ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG to find the parsing logic.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_202610080014167a3726ddabfd4540\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7227980533790142531\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7227980533790142531\",\"name\":\"read_object\",\"status\":