{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791389665,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_2026100800142033a2339fe202498c\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: outline(name), read_method(name, method, class), write_method(name, method, source - one METHOD block, class), read_object(name, include main|testclasses), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: prefer outline, read_method and write_method for changing existing methods; use write_source only for new methods, changed declarations or a new test include, and then write the FULL source; read before write; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG (settings from pia.env), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"The cause: get_from reads the value as everything after `=`, including trailing comments like ` # optional`. Also PIA_TURN_MODE value would be `job # optional: job | daemon | inline` which doesn't match \\\"job\\\" so turn mode setting is effectively ignored.\\n\\nFix: strip inline comments (everything from ` #` onwards) and trim whitespace.\\n\\nLet me look at the testclasses include first, if any.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_2026100800142033a2339fe202498c\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"content\":[{\"annotations\":[],\"text\":\"Found the cause already: `get_from` takes everything after `=` as the value \u2014 an inline comment ` # optional` becomes part of the value. Let me check the existing test include.\",\"type\":\"output_text\"}],\"id\":\"msg_2026100800142033a2339fe202498c\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"message\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"include\\\":\\\"testclasses\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7227991425827204624\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7227991425827204624\",\"name\":\"read_object\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1939,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":1344},\"output_tokens\":150,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":86},\"total_tokens\":2089}}
{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791389704,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_2026100800142562df729692364292\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: outline(name), read_method(name, method, class), write_method(name, method, source - one METHOD block, class), read_object(name, include main|testclasses), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: prefer outline, read_method and write_method for changing existing methods; use write_source only for new methods, changed declarations or a new test include, and then write the FULL source; read before write; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG (settings from pia.env), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"No test include exists yet. I'll create one with a test that reproduces the bug: line `PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3 # optional` \u2014 value should be trimmed to `glm-5.3`.\\n\\nTo test without touching the real pia.env, I can make get_from testable. get_from is private static; I could make it \\\"FOR TESTING\\\" visible via a test friend. Options: add `LOCAL FRIENDS` in the test include (CLASS zcl_pia_00_config DEFINITION LOCAL FRIENDS ltc_config.). Then call get_from directly with a test file. But get_from reads a file from the server \u2014 I'd need to write a temp file. Alternatively, refactor parsing into a static method that takes a line and returns value, e.g. `parse_value( iv_line )`. That's the cleanest: bug is in get_from where the value substring is taken without stripping inline comments and without trimming.\\n\\nPlan:\\n1. First write test include with test that calls a new helper `value_of_line( iv_line = 'PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3 # optional' )` expecting `glm-5.3`. But that helper doesn't exist yet; the test would fail to activate? Actually ABAP Unit tests referencing nonexistent methods would cause activation error. Hmm, activation happens on the main class; test include is part of the class. If I add a test referencing a nonexistent method, activation fails with syntax error. That's a problem for \\\"red\\\" test demonstration.\\n\\nAlternative: make the test drive the actual code path without new methods: use a test double by writing a real file? OPEN DATASET with a temp file is possible: create file via OPEN DATASET ... FOR OUTPUT in the test, write lines, then call get_from (needs friend access since private). LOCAL FRIENDS allows access to private methods. So:\\n\\n- test include: `CLASS ltcl_config DEFINITION FOR TESTING ... FRIENDS zcl_pia_00_config` \u2014 wait, friend declaration is in the class definition side: `CLASS zcl_pia_00_config DEFINITION LOCAL FRIENDS ltcl_...` placed in test include. Then test can call zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003eget_from.\\n\\nBut get_from reads file from server filesystem; writing a test file to DIR_HOME may not be allowed. Could pass a full path from TEMP dir. That's risky.\\n\\nBetter approach: the \\\"red\\\" requirement \u2014 I can write the test against existing behavior using the class's real get method but that reads real pia.env, non-deterministic.\\n\\nAlternative cleaner: refactor first (extract a pure static method `strip_comment`/`value_of` in private section), keep old buggy body calling it initially buggy. Hmm, but to get a red test first, I need a test that compiles and fails.\\n\\nApproach: Add to the class a private static method `value_of_line` implemented with the current (buggy) logic, have get_from call it. Test include with LOCAL FRIENDS calls value_of_line with `PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3 # optional` and asserts value = `glm-5.3`. Initially fails (red) because it returns `glm-5.3 # optional`. Then fix value_of_line to strip comments and trim. Test goes green.\\n\\nThat works and keeps production semantics unchanged initially. Steps:\\n\\nTurn 1: write_source main include with new private method value_of_line (buggy passthrough implementation) + test include. Activate. Turn 2: run_tests \u2192 red. Turn 3: fix value_of_line. Activate. Turn 4: run tests \u2192 green.\\n\\nActually I can combine: write main source and testclasses source in same turn (two write calls, independent? write_source to different includes of same class \u2014 independent targets, can be in same block). Then activate. Then run_tests next turn.\\n\\nAlso handle: trim leading/trailing blanks, strip inline comment `#...` but not if # inside value? For env files, values are simple; strip everything from first `#` (optionally preceded by whitespace). Also handle quoted values? README shows plain values. Keep it simple: cut at first `#`, trim. Also full-line comments starting with `#` and blank lines: currently FIND `=` fails \u2192 CONTINUE; a comment line containing `=` would be misparsed \u2014 key would be like `# something` not matching iv_name, fine.\\n\\nAlso trim leading blanks in value and trailing blanks. Let me write.\\n\\nvalue_of_line( iv_line ) RETURNING rv_: given line \\\"KEY=value stuff\\\", return the value part stripped of comments/whitespace. If no `=`, return initial. Implementation fix:\\n\\n```\\nMETHOD value_of_line.\\n  DATA lv_off TYPE i.\\n  DATA lv_val TYPE string.\\n  FIND FIRST OCCURRENCE OF `=` IN iv_line MATCH OFFSET lv_off.\\n  IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0.\\n    RETURN.\\n  ENDIF.\\n  lv_val = substring( val = iv_line off = lv_off + 1 ).\\n  \\\" cut inline comment\\n  FIND FIRST OCCURRENCE OF `#` IN lv_val MATCH OFFSET lv_off.\\n  IF sy-subrc = 0.\\n    lv_val = substring( val = lv_val len = lv_off ).\\n  ENDIF.\\n  rv_ = condense( lv_val ).\\nENDMETHOD.\\n```\\n\\ncondense removes leading/trailing and compresses inner multiple spaces to one \u2014 acceptable for env values.\\n\\nBug initially: rv_ = lv_val untrimmed.\\n\\nNow test class:\\n\\n```\\nCLASS ltcl_config DEFINITION FINAL FOR TESTING\\n  DURATION SHORT RISK LEVEL HARMLESS.\\n  PUBLIC SECTION.\\n    METHODS value_with_comment FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\n    METHODS value_plain FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\nENDCLASS.\\nCLASS zcl_pia_00_config DEFINITION LOCAL FRIENDS ltcl_config.\\nCLASS ltcl_config IMPLEMENTATION.\\n  METHOD value_with_comment.\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\n      exp = `glm-5.3`\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003evalue_of_line( `PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3 # optional` )\\n      msg = `inline comment must be stripped` ).\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\n      exp = `job`\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003evalue_of_line( `PIA_TURN_MODE=job # optional: job | daemon | inline` ) ).\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\n  METHOD value_plain.\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\n      exp = `glm-5.3`\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003evalue_of_line( `PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3` ) ).\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\nENDCLASS.\\n```\\n\\nNote: friend declaration must come before implementation? Order: `CLASS ltcl_config DEFINITION ... .` then `CLASS zcl_pia_00_config DEFINITION LOCAL FRIENDS ltcl_config.` then implementation. That works.\\n\\nFirst write main with buggy value_of_line so red run shows failure. Then activate. Next turn run_tests (red). Then fix, activate, run tests green.\\n\\nLet me write the main source now, keeping everything, adding value_of_line called from get_from, but initially buggy (raw substring). get_from still needs key comparison; I'll keep key extraction in get_from and use value_of_line for value? But value_of_line also does FIND =. Simpler: get_from keeps parsing loop; on match, rv_ = value_of_line( lv_line ). Buggy value_of_line returns raw substring after `=`. Good \u2014 behavior identical to today.\\n\\nWrite both includes in one block, then activate in next message? activate depends on writes, so must wait. Do: this turn two writes. Then activate. Then run tests.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_2026100800142562df729692364292\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"content\":[{\"annotations\":[],\"text\":\"I'll start by reading the config class (done above). The bug is visible: `get_from` takes everything after `=` as the value \u2014 an inline comment like ` # optional` becomes part of it (model name `glm-5.3 # optional`, and `PIA_TURN_MODE` mismatch). To make this testable without a real file, I'll extract a pure helper `value_of_line( iv_line )` (first with the current buggy behavior, so the test is red), plus a test include with LOCAL FRIENDS access.\",\"type\":\"output_text\"}],\"id\":\"msg_2026100800142562df729692364292\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"message\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"include\\\":\\\"main\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"CLASS zcl_pia_00_config DEFINITION PUBLIC FINAL CREATE PUBLIC.\\\\n\\\\n  PUBLIC SECTION.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" NAME=value lines; never committed. OSG: dir in OSD_DATASET_READ / OSD_DATASET_HOME.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" SAP: application server file (DIR_HOME or full path).\\\\n    CONSTANTS c_file TYPE string VALUE `pia.env`.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" settings without secrets (PIA_LLM, PIA_MODEL, PIA_TURN_MODE); read when pia.env has no value\\\\n    CONSTANTS c_settings TYPE string VALUE `pia-settings.env`.\\\\n\\\\n    CLASS-METHODS get\\\\n      IMPORTING iv_name    TYPE string\\\\n      RETURNING VALUE(rv_) TYPE string.\\\\n\\\\n    \\\\\\\" PIA_MODEL from pia.env, default glm-5.3 (glm-5.3-flash wrote invalid ABAP and empty tool args)\\\\n    CLASS-METHODS model\\\\n      RETURNING VALUE(rv_) TYPE string.\\\\n\\\\n  PRIVATE SECTION.\\\\n    CLASS-METHODS get_from\\\\n      IMPORTING iv_file    TYPE string\\\\n                iv_name    TYPE string\\\\n      RETURNING VALUE(rv_) TYPE string.\\\\n\\\\n    \\\\\\\" value part of a NAME=value line (pure helper, for unit tests)\\\\n    CLASS-METHODS value_of_line\\\\n      IMPORTING iv_line    TYPE string\\\\n      RETURNING VALUE(rv_) TYPE string.\\\\n\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\\n\\\\nCLASS zcl_pia_00_config IMPLEMENTATION.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD model.\\\\n    rv_ = get( `PIA_MODEL` ).\\\\n    IF rv_ IS INITIAL.\\\\n      rv_ = `glm-5.3`.\\\\n    ENDIF.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD get.\\\\n    rv_ = get_from( iv_file = c_file iv_name = iv_name ).\\\\n    IF rv_ IS INITIAL.\\\\n      rv_ = get_from( iv_file = c_settings iv_name = iv_name ).\\\\n    ENDIF.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD get_from.\\\\n    DATA lv_line TYPE string.\\\\n    DATA lv_key TYPE string.\\\\n    DATA lv_off TYPE i.\\\\n\\\\n    TRY.\\\\n        OPEN DATASET iv_file FOR INPUT IN TEXT MODE ENCODING UTF-8.\\\\n        IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0.\\\\n          RETURN.\\\\n        ENDIF.\\\\n        DO.\\\\n          READ DATASET iv_file INTO lv_line.\\\\n          IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0.\\\\n            EXIT.\\\\n          ENDIF.\\\\n          CLEAR lv_off.\\\\n          FIND FIRST OCCURRENCE OF `=` IN lv_line MATCH OFFSET lv_off.\\\\n          IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0.\\\\n            CONTINUE.\\\\n          ENDIF.\\\\n          lv_key = substring( val = lv_line len = lv_off ).\\\\n          IF lv_key = iv_name.\\\\n            rv_ = value_of_line( lv_line ).\\\\n            EXIT.\\\\n          ENDIF.\\\\n        ENDDO.\\\\n        CLOSE DATASET iv_file.\\\\n      CATCH cx_root.\\\\n        CLEAR rv_.\\\\n    ENDTRY.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD value_of_line.\\\\n    DATA lv_off TYPE i.\\\\n    FIND FIRST OCCURRENCE OF `=` IN iv_line MATCH OFFSET lv_off.\\\\n    IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0.\\\\n      RETURN.\\\\n    ENDIF.\\\\n    rv_ = substring( val = iv_line off = lv_off + 1 ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\\n\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7228034581658593022\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7228034581658593022\",\"name\":\"write_source\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"include\\\":\\\"testclasses\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"CLASS ltcl_config DEFINITION FINAL FOR TESTING\\\\n  DURATION SHORT RISK LEVEL HARMLESS.\\\\n\\\\n  PUBLIC SECTION.\\\\n    METHODS value_with_inline_comment FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\n    METHODS value_plain FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\n    METHODS line_without_equals FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\n\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\\n\\\\nCLASS zcl_pia_00_config DEFINITION LOCAL FRIENDS ltcl_config.\\\\n\\\\nCLASS ltcl_config IMPLEMENTATION.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD value_with_inline_comment.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" README style: value followed by a comment\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `glm-5.3`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003evalue_of_line( `PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3 # optional` )\\\\n      msg = `inline comment must be stripped from PIA_MODEL` ).\\\\n\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `job`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003evalue_of_line( `PIA_TURN_MODE=job # optional: job | daemon | inline` )\\\\n      msg = `inline comment must be stripped from PIA_TURN_MODE` ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD value_plain.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `glm-5.3`\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003evalue_of_line( `PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD line_without_equals.\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = ``\\\\n      act = zcl_pia_00_config=\\u003evalue_of_line( `# just a comment` ) ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\\n\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7228034581658593021\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7228034581658593021\",\"name\":\"write_source\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1968,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":1344},\"output_tokens\":2784,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":1618},\"total_tokens\":4752}}
