{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791389861,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_20261008001728929672f41d0c4fe9\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: outline(name), read_method(name, method, class), write_method(name, method, source - one METHOD block, class), read_object(name, include main|testclasses), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: prefer outline, read_method and write_method for changing existing methods; use write_source only for new methods, changed declarations or a new test include, and then write the FULL source; read before write; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG (settings from pia.env), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"All tests green. Let me also add a couple more edge-case tests? The task is essentially done: cause found, red test reproduced, fix applied, tests green. Maybe I should also add a test for a value with trailing spaces or a comment line starting with '#'. I could add tests for `PIA_LLM` URL with '#'? Unlikely. I think it's fine. Let me summarize.\\n\\nActually, let me double check one edge case: a full-line comment `# foo=bar` would be parsed as key `# foo` which never matches a name, so fine.\\n\\nAlso `PIA_TURN_MODE=job#optional` without space \u2014 README shows a space, and stripping unspaced '#' would risk breaking secrets that contain '#'. Keeping ' #' only is a reasonable choice. I could add a test documenting that decision. Let me quickly add one more test to lock behavior? Not strictly needed. The task says: reproduce red, fix, show green. Done. I'll finish with summary.\\n\\nActually it might be worth adding a test that a secret containing '#' (e.g., in an API key) survives \u2014 since that's a deliberate design choice of the fix. But careful: a key like `PIA_KEY=abc#123` keeps full value. With ' #' rule: `abc#123` has no ' #' so intact. And `PIA_KEY=abc #123`? Ambiguous. I'll keep it simple and finish.\\n\\nFinal answer in English (user wrote English), ending with PIA-DONE.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_20261008001728929672f41d0c4fe9\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"content\":[{\"annotations\":[],\"text\":\"Done. Summary of the work:\\n\\n**Cause** (in `ZCL_PIA_00_CONFIG=\\u003eGET_FROM`): the parser split each `pia.env` line at the first `=` and used everything after it verbatim as the value. A README-style inline comment therefore became part of the value:\\n- `PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3 # optional` \u2192 model `glm-5.3 # optional` sent to z.ai\\n- `PIA_TURN_MODE=job # optional: job | daemon | inline` \u2192 `job # optional: ...`, which matched none of the valid modes, so the setting was ignored.\\n\\n**Red test**: I extracted the value parsing into a testable private helper `VALUE_OF_LINE` and added local test class `LTCL_CONFIG` with `VALUE_WITH_INLINE_COMMENT` (asserting `glm-5.3` and `job`), `VALUE_PLAIN` and `LINE_WITHOUT_EQUALS`. Result before the fix: **1 fail** (`Expected [glm-5.3] / Actual [glm-5.3 # optional]`), 2 pass.\\n\\n**Fix** in `VALUE_OF_LINE` (now also used by `GET_FROM`): after cutting at the first `=`, everything from the first blank-hash (` #`) is stripped as an inline comment and the result is `CONDENSE`d. I deliberately cut only at ` #` (not bare `#`) so secrets that legitimately contain `#` without a leading space stay intact, and values without comments are unchanged.\\n\\n**Result**: tests now **green** \u2014 3 methods, 3 pass, 0 fail / 0 error. With this, `PIA_MODEL=glm-5.3 # optional` yields model `glm-5.3` and `PIA_TURN_MODE=job # optional: ...` yields `job`, so the turn mode is honored again.\\n\\nPIA-DONE\",\"type\":\"output_text\"}],\"id\":\"msg_20261008001728929672f41d0c4fe9\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"message\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":5908,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":3136},\"output_tokens\":715,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":316},\"total_tokens\":6623}}
